;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; THREE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (KEPCO is a
;;     foreign private issuer, NYSE ticker KEP, CIK 0000887225)
;;   * the issuer itself, at the Legal Notice page this repository archives
;;
;; WHY THE KOREAN REGISTER OF RECORD IS NOT CITED. GLEIF names RA000657 -- the
;; National Tax Service (국세청) Business registration -- as BOTH the register of
;; record and the validation authority for this entity (rows gleif-registered-at
;; and gleif-validated-at). That register publishes no per-entity GET URL:
;; www.nts.go.kr answers HTTP 200 at its root (checked 2026-08-22) but carries no
;; record data there, and the business-registration status lookup runs behind
;; Hometax POST/session flows this gate cannot replay. DART (dart.fss.or.kr) was
;; considered and not cited: its root answers 200, but per-entity data sits behind
;; POST search or the keyed OpenDART API, and a search page that echoes the query
;; is not a citation. So the entity's own Korean registration (120-82-00052)
;; rests on GLEIF alone. What the catalog does instead is corroborate the entity
;; through a second STATE authority that does answer on stable URLs:
;;
;;   GLEIF says the legal seat is 전력로 55, Naju-si, postal 58322 (rows
;;   gleif-address-jeollyeok, gleif-city, gleif-postal) -> the SEC prints
;;   55 JEOLLYEOK-RO, NAJU-SI, 58322 in its own business-address record
;;   (rows sec-street, sec-city, sec-zip). GLEIF records the English name
;;   KOREA ELECTRIC POWER CORPORATION -> EDGAR prints the same full name in its
;;   formerNames record, and prints KOREA ELECTRIC POWER CORP as the current
;;   registrant name. The SEC and GLEIF never consulted each other.
;;
;; ONE NAME, TWO ENCODINGS. GLEIF returns the Korean legal name 한국전력공사 as
;; \uXXXX escapes -- the Hangul bytes occur NOWHERE in the GLEIF response, so the
;; gleif-legal-name-korean row matches the escape sequence. The issuer's own page
;; serves the same name as raw UTF-8, so the issuer-* rows match the Hangul
;; directly. Expecting the wrong encoding on either URL would fail; both rows
;; keep that fact checked.
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's nextRenewalDate moves every year by
;; construction; a row on it would go red on schedule while saying nothing about
;; the entity, so it is left out. The KRX listing (ticker 015760, recorded in
;; blueprint.edn) is not cited: KRX market data sits behind POST APIs.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before
;; the claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or a specific
;;               related legal entity. Point the URL at a different company and
;;               the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT (status
;;               ACTIVE, country KR, city Naju-si, SIC 4911). Such a row can
;;               survive a swap to a similar company. It is recorded because it
;;               is checked and true, not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the row resolves a code used by another row (RA000657, WUJC).
;;               It says the named register or legal form exists; it says
;;               nothing about KEPCO.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 30 are :identity, 23 are :attribute and 8 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 61 as identifying would overstate what
;; this catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body and were each checked against
;; the fetched bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22, GLEIF golden copy
;; of 2026-08-21). The child-count and isin-count rows go red when GLEIF adds or
;; removes a relationship; that is correct DRIFT, not a false alarm.
